→ `2 failed` (`test_trusted_exact_invocation_takes_precedence_over_in_progress_rows`,
`test_dev_activates_a_named_pending_task_through_the_canonical_ledger_write`).

Repair: `current_task_selection` now validates `trusted_task_id` before any
`in_progress` handling — the invocation-local id resolves a dependency-ready
`pending` row even when another task is the unique `in_progress` (probe A) and
resolves a named row among multiple `in_progress` rows without emitting
`task_in_progress_ambiguous` (probe B); unknown / completed / dependency-blocked ids
keep their typed rejections and never silently select another task; nothing is
persisted. `skills/ultra-dev/SKILL.md` now requires the canonical activation — write
the named `pending` row to `in_progress` in `.ultra/tasks.json` and read it back
before the first implementation edit — with no selector, activation flag, or
workflow state.

